---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/region';
---

<Base
  title={`Terms & Disclaimer | ${SITE.shortName}`}
  description="Base Impact is a navigator, not a provider. These terms explain what we do, what we don't do, and your responsibilities when using this site."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="mb-6 text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Terms &amp; Disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">Last updated: {new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'long', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric' })}</p>

    <section class="mb-10 space-y-6 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed dark:text-slate-300">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Base Impact Inc. is a Florida nonprofit corporation, filed with the Florida Division of
        Corporations and registered with the Florida Department of Agriculture and Consumer
        Services. We are completing our founding board of directors, after which we will apply for
        501(c)(3) tax-exempt status. Until that status is granted, donations made directly to
        Base Impact Inc. are <strong>not tax-deductible</strong>. We operate a free local resource
        guide for Florida's Space Coast (Brevard, Volusia, Indian River, Orange, and Flagler
        counties).
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">We are a navigator, not a provider</h2>
      <p>
        Base Impact does not provide medical, mental health, legal, housing, or
        employment services. We do not operate, manage, own, or endorse any
        provider listed on this site. We route people to licensed gatekeepers —
        government agencies, 211, SAMHSA, AHCA, HUD, SSA, and local
        organizations. A listing is not an endorsement, and listing does not mean
        we recommend a particular level of care.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">No compensation — ever</h2>
      <p>
        Base Impact accepts <strong>zero compensation</strong> for any listing or
        referral — in any form: money, gifts, services, or anything of value.
        This includes treatment providers, sober homes, recovery residences,
        insurance carriers, and government programs. This is required by Florida
        law (Fla. Stat. § 817.505 — Patient Brokering Act) and is a condition of
        every listing on this site.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">What you are responsible for</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li>Verify every listing yourself before relying on it — phone numbers,
          hours, eligibility, and availability change.</li>
        <li>Call ahead. Nothing on this site replaces a direct conversation with
          the organization.</li>
        <li>Do not use this site to make medical, legal, or housing decisions
          without consulting a licensed professional.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">No warranties</h2>
      <p>
        All listings are provided &ldquo;as is.&rdquo; We do not warrant that
        listings are accurate, complete, current, or available. We make no
        representation about the quality of care, safety, or legitimacy of any
        provider. In no event will Base Impact, its officers, volunteers, or
        contributors be liable for any claim arising from your use of this site.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Your data</h2>
      <p>
        We do not track, store, or sell your location, search terms, or
        submission data on help pages. The submission form collects only what
        you choose to give us, and we use it only to check and improve listings.
        See our <a href="/privacy" class="underline">privacy note</a> for details.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Third-party information</h2>
      <p>
        Listings on this site describe <strong>third-party organizations</strong>. We compile them
        from sources published by those organizations or by government agencies — an official
        website, a public Facebook page, or a government program page. We are not the author or
        publisher of that information, we do not control it, and it can change without notice.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where we record a source and the date we read it, that record exists so we can answer
        &ldquo;where did this come from?&rdquo; It is <strong>not</strong> a claim that we
        contacted, visited, or inspected the organization. Our{' '}
        <a href="/sources" class="underline">Sources page</a> lists where each listing came from.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Names and trademarks</h2>
      <p>
        Organization names, logos, and trademarks mentioned on this site belong to their
        respective owners. We use them only to identify the organization being described. A
        listing implies <strong>no affiliation, sponsorship, partnership, or endorsement</strong>
        by either party.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Removal requests</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>If you represent an organization listed here and want it removed, we will remove
        it — no reason required.</strong> Use the{' '}
        <a href="/removal" class="underline">removal request form</a>, or email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="underline">{SITE.email}</a> with the subject line
        &ldquo;Removal request&rdquo;. We acknowledge within 2 business days and remove within 5,
        sooner if you ask urgently. Our decision is not up for negotiation — it is your listing to
        withdraw.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by Florida law, Base Impact Inc., its directors, officers,
        volunteers, and contributors are <strong>not liable</strong> for any indirect, incidental,
        special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for any loss of profits, data, or goodwill,
        arising out of or relating to your use of this site or any organization listed on it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our total aggregate liability for any claim arising from this site will not exceed{' '}
        <strong>one hundred dollars ($100)</strong>. Because this is a free service, that is the
        limit of what we can be responsible for. Some jurisdictions do not allow certain
        limitations, so parts of this section may not apply to you.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Indemnification</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to hold harmless and indemnify Base Impact Inc. and its directors, officers,
        volunteers, and contributors from any claim, demand, loss, or expense (including reasonable
        attorneys&rsquo; fees) arising from your use of this site or your violation of these terms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the <strong>State of Florida</strong>, without
        regard to conflict-of-law principles. Any dispute arising from this site will be brought
        exclusively in the state or federal courts located in{' '}
        <strong>Brevard County, Florida</strong>, and you consent to venue and personal
        jurisdiction there.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Accessibility</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to meet <strong>WCAG 2.1 Level AA</strong>. The site is built mobile-first, with
        large touch targets and screen-reader support. If any part of this site is not usable for
        you, please{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="underline">tell us</a> and we will fix it or get
        you the information another way.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms at any time. Continued use of the site after
        changes means you accept them.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, corrections, or concerns?{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="font-semibold text-emerald-800 underline dark:text-emerald-400">
          {SITE.email}
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-amber-900 dark:border-amber-800 dark:text-amber-200 dark:bg-amber-950/40">
      <p class="mb-1 font-bold">Important</p>
      <p>
        If you are in crisis, this site is not the right place. Call{' '}
        <a href="tel:988" class="font-semibold underline">988</a> (Suicide &amp; Crisis
        Lifeline), <a href="tel:18006624357" class="font-semibold underline">1-800-662-HELP</a>{' '}
        (SAMHSA), or <a href="tel:211" class="font-semibold underline">211</a> (United Way).
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
